  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThursday night through Saturday night\nAssessment...high (>80%) confidence on additional rounds of rain.\nLow (<25%) confidence on where the heaviest rain will fall\n\nAs mentioned yesterday, the quasi-stationary front will vacillate \nacross the area as each low moves east from the Plains. Thursday \nnight into Friday night the overall signal suggests the main focus \nfor the heavier rain will be across Minnesota into Wisconsin. Under \nthis scenario temperatures would be warming up through the period \nbut PWATs increasing to near 2 inches will create very muggy \nconditions, especially Friday into Saturday.\n\nIF the overall large scale synoptic picture is correct, the better \nrain chances Thursday night into Friday and Friday night into \nSaturday are north of I-80.\n\nSaturday night another low is progged to push the front back to the \nsouth which would bring the better convergence, higher PWATs and \nthus better chances for heavy rain back over the area.\n\nSunday-Wednesday...A surface pressure over Ontario pushes the \nlow pressure over Iowa southward into Missouri as the shortwave \nover the western CONUS finally propagates eastward. Mid-level \nCVA from the trough should support storm development north of \nthe low pressure Sunday into Monday before the system moves into\nIllinois and Indiana. CAA to kick in as the trough swings \nthrough the area, leading to a decrease in PoPs Tuesday and \nallowing cooler, drier air to move in.",
